From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:43:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [QW38] gdn recover fold: deferred commit into the next verify
 (D1, VLLM_GDN_RECOVER_FOLD=1)

VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE=recover (W = 1) folds each step's accepted records in a
post-sampling commit that re-reads and re-writes every state (verify R +
commit R+W per step). With VLLM_GDN_RECOVER_FOLD=1 the post-sampling commit
only records (ring half, accepted count) per request; the next verify folds
those records in registers (same replay and int16 quantizer), stores the
committed state in place, continues from the exact reload values and writes
this step's records into the other ring half: R+W per step, no commit pass.

- Records: per-layer side buffer keyed by the runner's request-table row
  (CommonAttentionMetadata.req_idx; mamba_hybrid now passes it), R = 2(k+1).
- Trackers per cache group; reset at request admission (add_request) and for
  non-spec (prefill) rows; a missing req_idx is a hard error.
- Align mode: rows whose accepted tokens reach a block boundary are still
  folded eagerly after sampling (boundary block + running state complete
  before caching/migration), via the commit kernel with a record row in the
  plan.
- Off by default. Test: tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py
  (bit-exact vs the eager commit over multi-step simulations).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
